body:
### Description

The `Build & Test (windows-11-arm)` job now fails on every PR while compiling `tests/core/metric/uniform_uint8_metric_test.cc`: MSVC crashes with an internal compiler error (C1001). It started when the `windows-11-arm` runner image upgraded MSVC from 14.44.35207, which passed (e.g. #780), to 14.51.36231. Examples: #773, #785, #787.

The trigger is the accumulation loop in the test helper `EncodeRecord`:

```cpp
sum_squared += static_cast<int>(codes[i]) * codes[i];   // int64_t sum_squared
```

The crash happens once this function is inlined into callers that pass constant-filled vectors. The function compiles fine by itself.

Expected: the test compiles on the current runner image.

### Steps to Reproduce

Minimal repro on Compiler Explorer, compiler `arm64 msvc v19.51 VS18.6` (also `v19.latest`), flags `/DNDEBUG /O2 /Ob2 /EHsc -std:c++17 -MT /Zc:preprocessor /Zc:__cplusplus /W3`:

```cpp
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstring>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdio>
namespace {
constexpr size_t kTailBytes = sizeof(uint32_t);
std::vector<int8_t> EncodeRecord(const std::vector<uint8_t> &codes) {
  std::vector<int8_t> encoded(codes.size() + kTailBytes, 0);
  int64_t sum_squared = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < codes.size(); ++i) {
    encoded[i] = static_cast<int8_t>(static_cast<int>(codes[i]) - 128);
    sum_squared += static_cast<int>(codes[i]) * codes[i];
  }
  const uint32_t tail = static_cast<uint32_t>(sum_squared);
  std::memcpy(encoded.data() + codes.size(), &tail, sizeof(tail));
  return encoded;
}
}
void t() {
  constexpr size_t kDimension = 4096;
  auto verify = [&](uint8_t a, uint8_t b) {
    const std::vector<uint8_t> rc(kDimension, a), qc(kDimension, b);
    auto r = EncodeRecord(rc); auto q = EncodeRecord(qc);
    printf("%d %d\n", r[0], q[1]);
  };
  verify(255, 0); verify(0, 255);
}
```

→ `fatal error C1001: Internal compiler error.` The same code compiles cleanly on `arm64 msvc v19.44`.

Changing the multiplication to `static_cast<int64_t>(codes[i]) * codes[i]` avoids the ICE without changing the result. A `#pragma loop(no_vector)` or splitting the loop also avoids it.

### Logs / Stack Trace

```shell
C:\a\zvec\zvec\tests\core\metric\uniform_uint8_metric_test.cc(37) : fatal error C1001: Internal compiler error.
(compiler file 'D:\a\_work\1\s\src\vctools\Compiler\Utc\src\p2\main.cpp', line 262)
  cl!UtcBldCompileSerializedFile()+0x3102d4
  ...
ninja: build stopped: subcommand failed.
```

https://github.com/alibaba/zvec/actions/runs/36823539790/job/113249486786

### Operating System

Windows 11 ARM64 (GitHub-hosted `windows-11-arm` runner)

### Build & Runtime Environment

MSVC 14.51.36231 (cl 19.51, VS 18 Enterprise, HostARM64/arm64), Ninja, Release (`/O2 /Ob2`), `ENABLE_WERROR=ON`, Python 3.11.9

### Additional Context

- [x] I've checked `git status` — no uncommitted submodule changes (seen on the CI's clean `actions/checkout`)
- [ ] I built with `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug` — no: Release flags (`/O2 /Ob2`); the bug is in the optimizer
- [ ] This occurs with or without `COVERAGE=ON` — not tried; the Windows job doesn't use coverage
- [ ] The issue involves Python ↔ C++ integration (pybind11) — no: C++ test compile only
